<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Komenda Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1694">1694</a>–<a href="/years/1700">1700</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/komenda">Komenda</a> Wars were a series of conflicts from 1694 to 1700 on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a>, centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> kingdom of Eguafo and its port of Komenda. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a> and the English Royal African Company backed rival local rulers and allies, including the merchant John Cabess, in a struggle for control of the trade in gold and slaves.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/komenda-wars.jpg" alt="Komenda Wars" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: G. Child · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Forts_at_Komenda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
